  "node_type": "statement",
  "body": {
    "kind": "theorem",
    "statement": "For every sufficiently large \\(N\\), there are Borel laws \\(P_{0,N},P_{1,N}\\in\\mathcal M_{\\mathrm{col}}\\subseteq\\mathcal M_\\star\\) and \\(s_N=1/(600\\log N)\\) such that \\(\\Gamma(P_{0,N})=\\Gamma(0)\\), \\(\\Gamma(P_{1,N})=\\Gamma(s_N)\\), and \\(\\|P_{0,N}^{\\otimes N}-P_{1,N}^{\\otimes N}\\|_{\\mathrm{TV}}\\to0\\).  Both laws have a one-dimensional, unit-variance, Gaussian-indecomposable source representation with \\(\\operatorname{rank}(A)=1\\) and \\(\\|A\\|_{\\mathrm{op}}<3\\), obey \\(q_u=2\\) on every \\(u\\in\\mathcal R\\) with common lower envelope constant \\(2/5\\) and upper envelope constant \\(60\\), satisfy \\(\\mathbb E\\|X\\|^8\\le M_8=50000000\\), and have the displayed covariance as their greatest Gaussian-divisor covariance.  Moreover,\n\\[\n \\Theta_{TY}(\\Gamma(P_{0,N}),\\preceq)=\\{b(0)\\},\\qquad\n \\Theta_{TY}(\\Gamma(P_{1,N}),\\preceq)=\\{b(s_N)\\}.\n\\]",
    "id": "thm:resolve-c157b16ef04ad06d0253",
